<h2>The rules</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Blackjack pays {{ blackjackOdds.blackjackPayoutStr }}.</b> A natural 21 on your first two cards, unless the dealer also has one, in which case it pushes.</li>
  <li><b>Dealer stands on all 17s</b>, including soft 17. The dealer peeks for blackjack immediately when showing an Ace or a 10-value card, before you have to act — so you're never risking extra money into a hand the dealer's already won.</li>
  <li><b>Double down</b> on any first two cards, including after a split: double your bet, take exactly one more card, done.</li>
  <li><b>Split</b> a matching-rank pair into two hands of equal size. One split per hand, no resplitting. Split aces get exactly one card each and can't be hit again.</li>
  <li><b>Insurance</b>, offered only when the dealer shows an Ace, costs half your bet and pays {{ blackjackOdds.insurancePayoutStr }} if the dealer has blackjack. It's a side bet on the dealer's hole card, not a hedge on yours — mathematically one of the worse bets you can make, same as it is at a real table.</li>
  <li><b>Push returns your bet</b> with no win or loss.</li>
</ul>

